<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Jan-July trade deficit CZK 85.3 bln.</title>
<headline>Czech Jan-July trade deficit CZK 85.3 bln.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech foreign trade deficit for January-July widened to 85.28 billion crowns from a revised deficit for the first half of the year of 68.87 billion crowns, the Czech Statistical Bureau (CSU) said on Monday.  </p>
<p> CZECH FOREIGN TRADE  JAN-JULY	JAN-JUNE     JAN-JULY '95</p>
<p>  imports (CZK bln)    429.901    363.58 (364.35)    371.002</p>
<p>  exports		  344.624    294.71 (294.62)    321.495</p>
<p>  balance		  -85.277    -68.87 (-69.73)    -49.507</p>
<p>Note. Figures are in billions of crowns on a customs- cleared basis. 1996 results use a different methodology than in 1995. Jan-June 1996 results are revised from earlier CSU report. Previously reported figures are in brackets.  </p>
<p>  (JANUARY-JULY PERIOD)     imports	 exports   balance</p>
<p>  By product groups		(in billions of crowns)</p>
<p>Agricultural products</p>
<p>  and foodstuffs		 29.845	  18.248   -11.597</p>
<p>Raw materials, unprocessed goods</p>
<p>  and chemical products     187.971	 165.898   -22.073</p>
<p>Machinery and</p>
<p>  transport equipment	 164.925	 112.461   -52.464</p>
<p>Industrial consumer</p>
<p>  products			 47.160	  48.017     0.857</p>
<p>  Total			   429.901	 344.624   -85.277</p>
<p>  Total index 1996/95 (pct) 115.9	   107.2</p>
<p>  BY TERRITORY		   imports	exports     balance</p>
<p>					(in billions of crowns)</p>
<p>Countries with a</p>
<p>  developed market economy    304.321     220.727     -83.594</p>
<p>   of that: EU countries	270.482     203.875     -66.607</p>
<p>  Developing countries	   21.268	20.466	  -802</p>
<p>European countries with transitional economy, and</p>
<p>  CIS countries		    99.711     101.422	 1.711</p>
<p>Other countries with transitional or state</p>
<p>  economies			   4.292	 1.659	-2.633</p>
<p>  Unspecified countries	   0.309	 0.350	 0.041</p>
<p>  Total			     429.901     344.624     -85.277</p>
<p>   of that: OECD countries    306.781     221.812     -84.969</p>
<p>Note. All figures in billions of crowns on customs-cleared basis.</p>
<p>-- Alan Crosby, Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
